<title>GERMANY: Thyssen shares boosted by H1 earnings.</title>
<headline>Thyssen shares boosted by H1 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German steel group Thyssen AG advanced on Tuesday after the company reported a stronger than expected 81 percent rise in its first-half pre-tax profit.</p>
<p>Thyssen hit a high of 404 marks on the news and was up 7.50 marks, or 1.9 percent, at 401 marks at 0823 GMT while the IBIS DAX index was flat at 3,674.09 points.</p>
<p>&quot;These were excellent numbers,&quot; said one dealer, noting that the report had given the whole market a lift in early trade.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 746525</p>
